      "message": "Thanks. As you might have guessed, I added this test to see if Steven\u0027s idea (setting \"target:{apex:{enabled:false}}\" instead of \"no_apex:true\" to avoid being included in apex bundles) would work.\n\nbtw, I found that \"depending on disabled module\" only emits error if \"VisitDeps*\" method is called in \"GenerateAndroidBuildActions()\". So, if a module walks dependency tree using an alternative (\"WalkDeps\" method), error is not emitted. \"apex\" module belongs to this case. So I want to keep this in cc_test with another test for apex in apex_test.\n\n(I guess that there are some reasons why \"WalkDeps\" is more permissive than \"VisitDeps*\" methods. )\n\nWhat do you think?",
