      "side": 1,
      "message": "target.apex.enabled is completely different from enabled. The former is not interpreted by module.go.\n\nImplementing the concept of no_apex by disabling the apex variant of the module might work, but personally I don\u0027t see a good value there.\n\n\u003e btw, I found that \"depending on disabled module\" only emits error if \"VisitDeps*\" method is called in \"GenerateAndroidBuildActions()\".\n\nReally? That sounds like a bug to me. BTW, I see validateAndroidModule is called inside WalkDeps.\n\nMaybe you are talking about WalkDepsBlueprint, which is a blueprint thing where \u0027enabled\u0027 does not exist.\n\nI originally used WalkDeps in apex.go, but after 778127a04192ffcf6df443f253e8a69868e3c529, allight@ changed it to WalkDepsBlueprint to be able to detect bootstrap.GoBinaryTool. I think we just need to make it back to WalkDeps.",
